[2025-04-15 21:50:32,630][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:50:32,630][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                    Timing attacks can exploit non-constant-time string comparison functions like `startsWith` to determine secrets character by character. Attackers can deduce when a guess&apos;s prefix matches part of the secret by measuring execution times over many trials, allowing them to crack an 8-character password in just thousands of attempts rather than billions. This can be demonstrated with a browser-based implementation using Thompson Sampling and a statistical approach. Developers should avoid direct secret comparisons and instead use proper cryptographic hashing with r"
[2025-04-15 21:50:32,635][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "ate limiting.[\n]"
[2025-04-15 21:50:32,635][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
