st by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.-QQnKmN9995ElcpR565Sh-SDvgyu6m58HhCZ9db8DGLU8eWWN6i18vkFYseYfcAZkjleDavofcd1QaJdy4QhXbvEZUoIayo57HzT-OKQaHuJTKD5OOItt_UfIrvcYdqIWu3s3rXJA6_TDOmqDqxJNiWrncR4OFTHh0NvNJ6_osn6dHS6Ec-X2xr15sltZmode359cWDYYQ4qscKpIk0VncYl7Rrdq9TjYBxwaOySrMAMW2HZwlnXaROOtzwUcsoBeIU50cznyikembc_Jld1X-89Re-auuzwfxiaLkaaYzIng3yE2jVsjEiELEpYXTPXAzMyIgXE9O0pYBqlgZGIYg/4ey/YDCb4n53TZe70uu_eMp2Gw/h44/h001.cWGyKTCYR-fg_XVrKvYwZzgLiTxHJkSXGoV2f6sErZQ&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ben Folland&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; on compromising threat actors[0xe2][0x80][0x99] Telegram-based command and control (C2) communications and analysing the data. Using VirusTotal, he found malware samples that communicate with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;api.telegram.org&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;, from he extracted Telegram bot tokens, which could then be used to forward hundreds of screenshots and keylogs from when the threat actor tested his payload on his production hacking box. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;This access allowed Ben to identify additional malspam campaigns being performed by this actor, the domains owned, email addresses used for services like Cloudflare and his VPS, and also all of the plaintext credentials used for the campaign[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s infrastructure. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&